{
  "id": "steam_control_valves___calculate_flow_factor_kv",
  "title": "Steam Control Valves - Calculate Flow Factor Kv",
  "description": "Calculator for determining the flow factor (Kv) for steam control valves using the formula: Kv = m / (31.7 * √(dP / v)). Based on pressure coefficient tables and steam flow specifications.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "id": "kv_calculator",
      "content": "## Steam Control Valve - Kv Calculator\n\nCalculate the flow factor (Kv) using the formula:\n\n**Kv = m / (31.7 × √(dP / v))**\n\nWhere:\n- m = steam flow (kg/h)\n- dP = pressure drop (bar)\n- v = specific volume of steam before valve (m³/kg)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "steam_flow_m",
          "label": "Steam Flow (m)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/h",
          "defaultValue": 100
        },
        {
          "id": "pressure_drop_dp",
          "label": "Pressure Drop (dP)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "bar",
          "defaultValue": 1.5
        },
        {
          "id": "specific_volume_v",
          "label": "Specific Volume of Steam (v)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m³/kg",
          "defaultValue": 0.19
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "flow_factor_kv",
          "label": "Flow Factor (Kv)",
          "formula": "inputs.steam_flow_m / (31.7 * Math.sqrt(inputs.pressure_drop_dp / inputs.specific_volume_v))",
          "unit": "",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "pressure_coefficient_guide",
      "content": "## Step 1: Determine Pressure Coefficient (Pcoef)\n\nThe pressure coefficient is determined from steam tables based on:\n- Absolute inlet pressure (bar)\n- Pressure drop across the valve (bar)\n\n**Important:** Pressure drop cannot exceed approximately 42% of inlet pressure (critical pressure drop).\n\n**Formula:** Pcoef = pressure drop / specific volume\n\n### Example\nFor 10 bar absolute pressure with 3.5 bar pressure drop:\n- Pcoef = 18.4 (from steam tables)"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "flow_factor_guide",
      "content": "## Step 2: Determine Flow Factor (Kv)\n\n1. Find the pressure coefficient (Pcoef) column closest to your calculated value\n2. Follow the column down to find your steam flow rate\n3. Interpolate between values if necessary\n4. Read the corresponding Kv value from the left column\n\n### Example\nFor Pcoef = 18.2 and steam flow = 592 kg/h:\n- **Flow Factor Kv = 4.4**"
    },
